## Implementation Plan: Agent Management Suite

### Overview

Five new browser-to-server message types, five new `handleBrowserMessage` switch cases, five new hook functions, and a right-click context menu on sidebar items. The design reuses existing server-side primitives (`killAgent`, `relaunchAgent`, `setAgentStatus`, `persistAgentSync`, `broadcastAgentList`, `store.remove`) wherever possible.

### Key Design Decision: Where Do Controls Live?

**A right-click context menu on each sidebar agent item.** This is the minimal, non-cluttered approach. The sidebar items already render as `<button>` elements; adding an `onContextMenu` handler is trivial. No changes to the Chat header are needed. The menu items are:

- Rename (always available)
- Relaunch (only when status is `disconnected`, `done`, or `error`)
- Kill (only when status is `spawning`, `connected`, or `thinking`)
- Clear History (always available)
- Delete (always available, with confirmation)

